                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2604ce6-9c55-3b58-b138-916e54ab4a3c",
                                        "entry_id": "356b8b98-60d5-3831-ac1f-4265852861cd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of adjudicating, of reaching a judgement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8168926-e3ee-490b-bbd5-80401591c021",
                                                "sense_id": "a2604ce6-9c55-3b58-b138-916e54ab4a3c",
                                                "text": "All too often nowadays, in the majority of cases, the commissioners have no familiarity at all with the case decided in their names, and do not even read the order they sign. Thus, the entire procedure of adjudication by the commission has become a farce and a travesty, which has outlived its usefulness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de74934b-d4f5-3ec1-9e70-96bf48290bad",
                                        "entry_id": "356b8b98-60d5-3831-ac1f-4265852861cd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A judgment or sentence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4aee00b-cd99-4cfa-b609-bc4bd41cd279",
                                                "sense_id": "de74934b-d4f5-3ec1-9e70-96bf48290bad",
                                                "text": "16 June, 1784, Edmund Burke, speech on reform of representation in the House of Commons\nAn adjudication in favour of natural rights."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae9b63aa-adfd-4149-bacf-e11bfa386928",
                                                "sense_id": "de74934b-d4f5-3ec1-9e70-96bf48290bad",
                                                "text": "[Mr. C.] says he confessed to avoid a lengthier sentence after his original attorney told him that the prosecutor claimed DNA evidence conclusively identified him as the attacker. [Mr. C.] had an earlier deferred adjudication for indecency with a minor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e7451a8-16e6-3b2b-817f-bcac78285480",
                                        "entry_id": "356b8b98-60d5-3831-ac1f-4265852861cd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The decision upon the question of whether the debtor is a bankrupt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdb8c435-cbdc-4a40-a98a-b4a14fe79b9b",
                                                "sense_id": "0e7451a8-16e6-3b2b-817f-bcac78285480",
                                                "text": "In case two or more petitions for adjudication of bankruptcy shall be filed in different districts by different members of the same copartnership for an adjudication of the bankruptcy of said copartnership , the court in which the petition is first filed having jurisdiction[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8689e605-12e3-3c85-baac-81ff7450ce5c",
                                        "entry_id": "356b8b98-60d5-3831-ac1f-4265852861cd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process of identifying the type of material or device that set off an alarm and assessing the potential threat with corresponding implications for the need to take further action."
                                        ],
